// Package adt is the Gom abstract-syntax-tree package, generated by the
// Go Gom itself (tom/gom/backend) from the five .gom files of this
// directory:
//
//	Code.gom  Gom.gom  Objects.gom  Rule.gom  SymbolTable.gom
//
// They are the Go compiler's own copies of the Java compiler's
// src/tom/gom/adt/*.gom: same sorts, operators and slots (checked by
// TestSignatureParity, tom/internal/adtgen), hooks written in Go (the
// HookList javablock of Objects.gom: ContainsTomCode, plain Go), so
// that the Go ASTs can evolve independently of the Java ones.
//
// This is the self-bootstrap of the Gom AST: the Go Gom parser and
// backend manipulate exactly the same abstract structures the reference
// Java Gom does. Importers conventionally alias it as gomast:
//
//	import gomast "tom/gom/adt"
//
// The package is generated as any Gom module (gomgo gom-batch): the
// Java Gom API (Get<slot>, Is<op>, GetHead<op>/GetTail<op>, Length,
// ToArray, CompareTo, ToATerm, <Sort>FromString, …), lists as
// maximally-shared cons cells, and the Tom mapping adt.tom. Every term
// lives in the shared-objects factory of this package; two structurally
// equal terms compare equal by pointer.
//
// # Regeneration
//
// From the repository root:
//
//	mage -d magefiles -w . regenAdt
//
// (go run ./internal/adtgen/regenadt in src/go/tom), which regenerates
// gom/adt, engine/adt and engine/adt/il. TestSelfBootstrap
// (tom/internal/adtgen) checks that the committed sources are
// byte-identical to a fresh regeneration — for this package, a fixpoint:
// gomgo, built on this package, regenerates it identically. The
// generated sources should NEVER be edited by hand — every change must
// go through the .gom sources and a clean regeneration.
package adt
